>>
Rule 1 (x and y must have the same type)
{x : tensor, y : tensor} |= dtype_(x) = dtype_(y)
>>
Rule 2 (x must be a floating-point or complex tensor)
{x : tensor} |= (dtype_(x) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 5) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(x) = 4)
>>
Rule 3 (y must be a floating-point or complex tensor)
{y : tensor} |= (dtype_(y) = 6) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 7) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 8) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 10) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 5) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 1) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 3) ∨ (dtype_(y) = 4)
>>
Rule 5 (x cannot be a bool tensor)
{x : tensor} |= dtype_(x) ≠ 0
